WEBVTT

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.410
We should be going home.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.370
Yes.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.160
Anne decides not to go to the university,
and remain in the house.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.750
When it becomes known to all of Avonlea
that she is to be a teacher,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.360
there is a good deal of discussion over it.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:25.700
Most of the good folks,
not knowing about Marilla's eyes,

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.100
thinks she is foolish and pities her.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.880
However, Mrs. Allan does not.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.130
She tells Anne so in approving words

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.120
that brings tears of
pleasure to the girl's eyes.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.370
One night, Anne and Marilla

00:02:54.380 --> 00:03:00.170
are sitting at the front door in
the warm, scented summer dusk.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.490
They like to sit there when the twilight comes down

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.420
and the white moths
fly about in the garden,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.220
and the odor of mint fills the dewy air.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.260
Sitting here has become a habit for them.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.000
- It's mint...
- What?

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.310
I smell mint.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:23.560
Yes.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.710
It's a nice smell.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.080
Yes. A nice smell.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.030
Oh! It's Mrs. Lynde.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.160
Good evening, Mrs. Lynde.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.040
Well, well. So you're here today as well?

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.810
You always seem to be in this place recently.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.270
Yes. It's all because of Anne's influence.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:05.460
I declare I'm getting glad to sit down.
I've been on my feet all day,

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:12.230
and two hundred pounds is a
good bit for two feet to carry round.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.470
It's a great blessing not to be fat, Marilla.
I hope you appreciate it.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.030
It may be so.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.270
Well, Anne. I hear you've given up
your notion of going to college.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.610
- I was real glad to hear it.
- Eh?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:31.120
You've got as much education now
as a woman can be comfortable with.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.500
I don't believe in girls going
to college with the men

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.890
and cramming their heads
full of Latin and Greek

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.710
and all that nonsense.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.890
But you know, Mrs. Lynde,

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.850
even though I'm not going to university,

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.430
I'm going to study Latin
and Greek just the same.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:47.410
What?

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.310
I'm going to take my Arts course
right here at Green Gables,

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.680
and study everything that I would at college.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.140
Anne Shirley, you'll kill yourself!

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.170
Not at all.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.820
Oh, I'm not going to overdo things.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:08.300
As 'Josiah Allan's wife,' says, I shall be 'mejum'.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:13.960
But I'll have lots of spare time
in the long winter evenings,

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.930
and I've no vocation for handicraft.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.030
I'm going to teach over at Carmody, you know.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.530
I wonder.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.540
I guess you're going to
teach right here in Avonlea.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.830
The trustees have decided
to give you the school.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.500
Mrs. Lynde!

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.780
Why, I thought they had promised it to Gilbert Blythe!

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.050
So they did. But as soon as Gilbert
heard that you had applied for it,

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.950
he went to them.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.840
They had a business meeting at
the school last night, you know.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.920
He told them that he withdrew his application,

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.060
and suggested that they accept yours.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:53.000
He said he was going
to teach at White Sands.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:58.470
It's obvious he gave it up for your sake.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:03.600
Of course he knew how much you
wanted to stay with Marilla.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:07.980
I must say I think he's real kind and thoughtful.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:11.010
Real self-sacrificing, too,

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.110
for he'll have his board to pay at White Sands,

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.250
And he's going to university, too, isn't he?

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.520
To that end, he must earn enough
for the school expenses.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.630
So the trustees decided to take you.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:35.410
I was so happy for you when
Thomas came home and told me.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.410
I don't feel that I should accept it.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.150
I don't think I ought to let Gilbert
make such a sacrifice for me.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.540
I guess you can't prevent him now.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:49.580
He's signed papers with the White Sands trustees.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.590
So it wouldn't do him any good
now if you were to refuse.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.310
Since he's gone to such pains,
you should stay and teach in Avonlea, Anne.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.670
You'll get along all right,
now that there are no Pyes in school.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.300
Josie was the last of them,
and it's a good thing she was.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.030
There's been some Pye or other

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.780
going to Avonlea school
for the last twenty years,

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.480
and I guess their mission in life

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:19.840
was to keep school teachers reminded
that earth isn't their home.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:21.550
Well, well.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:22.900
What?

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:26.250
What does all that winking and
blinking at the Barry gable mean?"

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.560
That's Diana's signal.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:29.030
Signal?

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.560
That's right. She wants
me to come right away.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.660
You know we keep up the old custom.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:38.070
Excuse me while I run over
and see what she wants.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.740
Don't come home too late.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:41.580
I won't!

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:51.610
There's a good deal of the child
about her yet in some ways.

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.280
So what?

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:57.280
There's a good deal more of the
woman about her in others.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.970
Marilla regains her crispness for a moment.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:07.340
But crispness is no longer
Marilla's distinguishing characteristic.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:11.360
As Mrs. Lynde tells her Thomas that night:

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:16.280
Marilla Cuthbert has got mellow. That's what.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.540
Meanwhile,
Anne is going to Diana's place.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:24.310
While she's walking through the "ghost forest",
rather than thinking of of Diana,

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:29.450
she's thinking of how to thank Gilbert Blythe
for the sacrifice has made for her sake.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:35.480
Diana sent the signal because
Miss Josephine Barry is visiting,

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.470
and because she says she must talk to Anne.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:46.500
Anne, I was shocked when Diana told me.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:50.420
I thought you had become an idiot.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.070
Isn't that so? After all
your struggle and effort...

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:59.260
No one understands
this more than I do.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.580
You finally get the scholarship
and then you throw it away.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:07.790
Now, now, Aunt Josephine.
Anne thought about it...

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.680
No, I really don't understand.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.990
You're not troubling anyone.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:17.600
You would be able to graduate from
university without having to pay a penny.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:22.140
What are you doing, giving up
such a good opportunity?

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.580
You'll regret it for life!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:28.480
I was shocked, too, when I heard, Anne.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:33.110
Everyone in Avonlea gave you their blessings
because it was such a prestigious scholarship.

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:35.220
It's really a pity.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:38.130
I don't care about this prestige.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.530
Tell me, Anne, why would
you do such a thing?

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:43.660
You don't want to go to university?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.000
If that's so, it can't be helped,

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:50.370
But I will not stay quiet if Marilla Cuthbert
asked you to give up university!

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.100
Aunt.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.200
Please don't interrupt!

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.680
Since Matthew passed away, there
may have been a lot to see to,

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.670
and I'm sure Marilla feels lonely.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:04.480
But compared to me,
Marilla is still young.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.950
Who doesn't grow old?

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:10.090
To get Anne, who's not even her
adopted daughter, to stay with her...

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.190
She's too selfish.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:15.160
And, most of all, it's unfair to you.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:20.470
Miss Barry, when Marilla first heard that
I was to give up the scholarship,

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:25.370
she was against it.
She didn't want me to sacrifice it for her.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:31.540
I went against her objections and chose
to take this course without permission.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:35.960
I don't regret it.
Actually, I'm glad I did that now.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.190
What?!

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:42.550
Because even Queen Victoria couldn't change my decision

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.820
to stay with Marilla at Green Gables.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.710
Even though I don't really understand the circumstances,

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:58.430
your expression tells me that
I'm too overly concerned.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:01.440
I was so worried and
called you here forcefully.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:08.130
Miss Barry, you have a kind heart.
To think you would worry so much for me...

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:13.680
I'll never let anyone down again.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.500
No matter what others may think of me,

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:21.470
this time, I get to see
what I didn't see in the past.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:25.700
The strength and warmth of a human heart.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:31.240
You've reminded me that I have this
unique opportunity to test my heart.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:36.580
Well, well. That's all right, then.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:42.940
You seem to have thought it through
and found compelling reasons.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.590
I will say no more.

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:49.150
Miss Barry...

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:59.530
Please give my best regards to Mr. Barry.
I'm indebted to him for taking over the fields.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:03.270
Not at all. Taking over them
has helped us survive.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.810
Well, Marilla's waiting for me.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.550
Good night, Diana.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:08.770
Good night, Anne.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:33.890
Anyway, Marilla must be very happy
to have a child like that by her side.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.970
I'm a little envious.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.340
Aunt Josephine.

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:31.450
Hello, Anne! Are you going
to the grave today again?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.580
Yes. I'm still worried about the rose cutting.

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:38.540
Oh, you have letters. Two of them.

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:40.590
Oh my! That many?

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:42.800
Look. Here they are.

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:43.560
Thank you.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:47.380
Oh! This is from Miss Stacy,
and this is from Stella.

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:49.440
Can I read them here?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.000
Go ahead.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:02.760
Dear Anne. I have a great announcement to make.

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:05.330
Yesterday, I got a notification
that I've been accepted

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:07.600
by Redmond University as you were.

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:12.690
When I thought that I
could study with you again,

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:16.730
I was very happy and immediately
wrote this letter to you.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:19.640
When will you come to Redmond?

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:24.440
Let me know once you have a date.
I'll pick you up at the station.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.450
Congratulations, Stella.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:53.990
Matthew, thanks to Gilbert Blythe,
I can teach at Avonlea school.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:58.040
This is my alma mater, after all.
I won't lose to Miss Stacy.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:01.240
I will do my best to become a good teacher.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.590
I'll come see you again.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:26.310
Miss Stacy's letter is,
just as Anne has expected,

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:30.440
a belated letter of congratulation
on getting the Avery scholarship.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.280
Reading the letter,

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:39.790
Anne remembers Miss Stacy
writing on the black board.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:40.660
Anne!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.220
It's you, Anne!

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.400
Mrs. Allan!

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:54.110
I see, but it's great that you
decided on Avonlea's school.

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:55.630
Yes, truly.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:59.220
There's one more thing I'm happy about.

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:04.000
It's that you, and all the others from
this school that went to Queen's,

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.990
have become teachers.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.920
If you all work together,

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:13.450
I expect you'll be the
youthful center of this village.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.460
Of course, you will
participate as well, won't you?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.360
Yes, gladly.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:58.270
Gilbert. I want to thank you for
giving up the school for me.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:03.800
It was very good of you, and I want
you to know that I appreciate it.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.970
It wasn't particularly good of me at all, Anne.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.040
I was pleased to be able to
do you some small service.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.880
Are we going to be friends after this?

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:15.280
Have you really forgiven me my old fault?

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:20.250
I forgave you that day by the pond landing,

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:22.480
although I didn't know it.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.490
What a stubborn little goose I was.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:28.600
I've been... I may as well
make a complete confession.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.780
I've been sorry ever since.

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:35.500
We are going to be the best of friends.

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:39.300
We were born to be good friends, Anne.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:41.550
You've thwarted destiny enough.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.070
You are going to keep up
your studies, aren't you?

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:46.790
Yes.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.430
I will, too. I know we can
help each other in many ways.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:52.440
I'm sure we can.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:53.950
Definitely!

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.480
Come, I'm going to walk home with you.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.000
Anne came back with a boy.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:36.420
But who was that?

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.920
I'm home. Sorry I'm late.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.460
Welcome home, Anne.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:14.390
Oh! You're doing evening work?

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.640
It's all right. Don't worry too much.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:21.090
I have Martin, and even
though my eyes are bad,

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:22.680
I want to keep doing things myself.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.850
Thank you, Marilla.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:32.020
By the way, Anne. Who was it that
came up the lane with you?

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.150
It was Gilbert Blythe.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.920
I thanked him for
giving up the school for me.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:41.460
I didn't think you and Gilbert Blythe were such good friends

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.630
that you'd stand for thirty
minutes at the gate talking to him.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:48.060
We haven't been. We've been good enemies.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:53.270
But we have decided that it would be
better to be good friends from now on.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:56.860
But... did we really stand
there for thirty minutes?

00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:58.530
Yes, you did.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.450
It seemed just a few minutes.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:07.320
But, you see, Marilla. We have five
years' lost conversations to catch up with.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:08.930
I guess so.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.030
Well, would you like some tea?

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:12.400
Yes.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:18.830
That night, after sending
Marilla to her bedroom,

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:24.600
Anne sits on the windowsill and writes
to Miss Stacy and Stella Maynard.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:33.480
While explaining her circumstances briefly,
she often rests her pen and thinks.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:39.690
A breeze moves quietly through the
large branches of the cherry tree,

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:42.280
carrying with it the scent of peppermint.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:47.480
Stars glitter above the forest.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.960
Between the leaves,

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:52.260
Anne can see Diana's light.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.590
My horizons have closed in

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.700
since the night I sat here
after coming home from Queen's.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.780
Perhaps they have closed in too much.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:10.580
But if the path set before
my feet is to be narrow,

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:15.960
I know that flowers of quiet
happiness will bloom along it.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:21.890
The joy of sincere work
and worthy aspiration

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:26.060
and true friendship is waiting for me.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:42.950
It's true that roads always
have forks, isn't it?

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:49.420
You never know what you'll
find after you've chosen your path.

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.780
I placed my hopes and
dreams in the hands of fate

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.050
and what it would bring
me after choosing a path.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:02.800
But meandering on this more
restrictive path in life has,

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:06.950
compared to when I just ran single-mindedly
toward the horizon in front of me,

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:10.240
allowed me to feel the warmth of the people around me,

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:14.110
and made the beauty that
surrounds me more plentiful.

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:18.570
Of course, I will not forget
the high mountains

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:21.490
towering on the other
side of the horizon.

00:22:22.330 --> 00:22:29.550
No one can take away the ideal world
that I've created with my imagination.

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:36.670
But I have no regrets now.

00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:40.900
Being filled with peace,
I can praise the splendor of this world.

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:45.710
Just like a that passage by Browning...

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:53.250
"God's in his Heaven.
All's right with the world"

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:08.830
namida ga koboretemo
Even if tears are falling

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:13.000
hitotsubu koboretemo
Even if one drop is falling

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:18.520
ima wa kaze ga fuiteiru
At this moment, the wind is blowing

00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:28.380
nobara no shigemi kara fuiteiru
Blowing from the wild rose patch

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:33.710
kagami wo mitara
When I look into the mirror

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:42.880
nobara to kaze ga utsutteiru
The wild rose and the wind is reflected

00:23:43.930 --> 00:23:52.660
namida wa mou kiete shimatte
The tears have already disappeared

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:10.820
Hey! Hey! I'm the scoundrel
of the world: Tom Sawyer!

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:13.570
Well, our first adventure is about to start!

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:18.870
In the first adventure, we're going
to catch a terribly huge pig!

00:24:19.070 --> 00:24:24.280
Since it's a wild pig,
it will be a great adventure!

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:27.750
The new series
"The Adventures of Tom Sawyer", episode 1:

00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:30.030
Tom, Huck and the Pig Riot

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:31.410
Please watch it!
